A||||18||ChopTop||Photopoint side ground effects request||||1||
Z||000000||ChopTop||09-26-2001||11:50 AM||||Pontiac did a great job in designing the aero nose and rear bumper covers on  the GT Fiero, but not as well on the side ground effects.  The side ground effects pieces look tacked on, and I guess they should since that is essentially what they are.  I wished Pontiac had opted to spend the extra money to design a side ground package that would have matched the lower portion of the molded in ground effect design of the GT covers.  They did it with the Pontiac Trans Am of the 82 to 92 period, and the GTZ Beretta.  I would like to see what it would look like on the GT Fiero.<BR>Basically I would like to see the four ground effects pieces turned into two.  The lower door piece would be one, and then merge the rocker piece and two trim pieces into one design.  Would someone with Photopoint skills take the side view of a GT and make it look the way Pontiac should have designed in the first place.  Thanks in advance!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leper||09-26-2001||05:28 PM||||DGP made a great lookng set of rocker panels for the coupe.<BR>They probably won't look very integrated with the aero fascias, but they look very good on the car.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home.mindspring.com/~hartzfeld/_uimages/overheadsm.jpg"> <BR>If the pic doesn't show <A HREF="http://home.mindspring.com/~hartzfeld/_wsn/page3.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.mindspring.com/~hartzfeld/_wsn/page3.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leper||09-26-2001||05:31 PM||||Thank Hartz for the picture.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChopTop||09-27-2001||10:28 AM||||Well..I was hoping someone with Photopoint skills would use the stock ground effects to get the look I'm thinking of.||||reg||1
